# Gate mode item eqy_rtl: the netlist (Yosys view exp_lut_fv.v: netlist + combinational PDK
# models + liberty flop models) against the golden RTL (snapshot/exp_lut.v) at the same
# REGISTERED value (@REG@ is replaced by run_all.sh). Strategy sat, depth 1.
#   REGISTERED = 0: no state; each partition is a combinational function of the inputs, so
#     PASS is a complete combinational equivalence.
#   REGISTERED = 1: the 9 state bits are matched by name (they drive the outputs W and done
#     directly in both designs); each partition's next-state and output functions are
#     proven equal, an unbounded equivalence proof. A netlist that re-encodes the state so
#     that no name match exists gives "equivalence unknown" (failed) and would need its own
#     reviewed match.
# proc -norom: case tables stay logic; EQY's sat strategy skips partitions that contain a
# memory (the golden's weight table would otherwise become a ROM, "No configured strategy").
[gold]
read_verilog -sv gold.v
chparam -set REGISTERED @REG@ exp_lut
hierarchy -top exp_lut
proc -norom
prep -top exp_lut

[gate]
read_verilog gate.v
hierarchy -top exp_lut
proc -norom; flatten; opt_clean
prep -top exp_lut

[strategy sat]
use sat
depth 1
